WEBVTT

00:36.161 --> 00:38.955
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

00:40.707 --> 00:44.169
Before enlisting, I had five million won,

00:44.252 --> 00:46.171
so I put it into stocks.

00:46.796 --> 00:47.964
When I got discharged…

00:48.047 --> 00:49.215
Ta-da.

00:49.883 --> 00:51.593
It increased to 30 million.

00:52.635 --> 00:53.511
Yes, 30 million.

00:54.512 --> 00:55.722
Right then,

00:55.805 --> 00:57.724
do you know what my biggest worry was?

00:59.225 --> 01:01.227
"I'm the only one
who knows about this money."

01:02.187 --> 01:03.396
"What if I die?"

01:05.648 --> 01:06.649
Then one day…

01:08.818 --> 01:10.070
a burglar tried to break in.

01:12.781 --> 01:14.449
I saw something like a knife,

01:15.283 --> 01:16.993
and my heart started pounding.

01:17.911 --> 01:18.912
I didn't know what to do.

01:20.080 --> 01:21.247
At that moment,

01:21.331 --> 01:23.750
I thought of the 30 million won I had.

01:31.007 --> 01:31.883
I thought, "I can't die."

01:32.801 --> 01:34.302
"I have 30 million won."

01:35.929 --> 01:39.265
Even though I hadn't eaten or slept,

01:39.349 --> 01:40.600
I was full of energy.

01:41.893 --> 01:43.269
That 30 million won

01:43.353 --> 01:45.438
made me feel like I had superpowers.

01:47.899 --> 01:48.942
But then…

01:51.653 --> 01:53.154
it increased to 50 million won.

02:08.086 --> 02:09.045
Suddenly,

02:09.587 --> 02:11.464
everything became easy.

02:13.758 --> 02:17.428
It felt like
nothing in life stood in my way.

02:20.223 --> 02:21.099
Dong-man.

02:23.309 --> 02:24.936
Let's step into the center…

02:27.814 --> 02:28.731
of history.

02:37.448 --> 02:38.324
Hey, Hwang.

02:39.075 --> 02:40.034
Want to try taking a photo?

02:44.831 --> 02:47.000
You were such a beautiful young man.

02:48.209 --> 02:49.377
I'll bear that in mind.

02:49.460 --> 02:51.713
I can see the universe in your face.

02:52.463 --> 02:54.465
From what angle and in what way

02:54.549 --> 02:57.385
can I capture
the depth of the universe inside you?

02:57.969 --> 03:01.472
I ponder over this every day
while watching all of your films.

03:01.556 --> 03:02.724
He really is a crazy bastard.

03:02.807 --> 03:04.017
After watching you every day,

03:04.100 --> 03:07.020
I'm beginning to mix up your face

03:07.103 --> 03:08.354
with mine.

03:09.856 --> 03:12.442
HWANG DONG-MAN: HEHEHE

03:12.525 --> 03:14.986
Seriously, this little punk.

03:17.030 --> 03:17.906
MR. NOH KANG-SIK

03:17.989 --> 03:19.198
Stop messaging me.

03:21.367 --> 03:22.911
Who does he think he is?

03:22.994 --> 03:25.413
How dare you have the audacity
to babble on like that?

03:25.496 --> 03:26.331
Yes, sir!

03:26.414 --> 03:27.665
I got excited

03:27.749 --> 03:30.501
because I have the top actor Noh Kang-sik
in my contacts.

03:30.585 --> 03:31.419
Damn it.

03:31.502 --> 03:32.795
That's it for today.

03:33.504 --> 03:34.547
Jeez.

03:36.257 --> 03:38.051
Director, let's take five.

04:03.826 --> 04:05.536
DEPOSIT AMOUNT: 20,000,000 WON
SENDER: HWANG DONG-MAN

04:05.620 --> 04:06.579
What's this?

04:07.288 --> 04:08.373
You're saving 100 million won

04:09.791 --> 04:11.000
to give Yeong-sil when you see her.

04:12.669 --> 04:13.670
I'm going to chip in.

04:14.754 --> 04:15.797
I got my signing fee.

04:17.006 --> 04:18.258
My film's going into production.

04:28.017 --> 04:29.143
DEPOSIT AMOUNT: 20,000,000 WON
SENDER: HWANG JIN-MAN

04:29.227 --> 04:30.353
Why?

04:31.145 --> 04:33.106
If you have money,
get your own place and move out.

04:33.690 --> 04:34.732
Live your own life,

04:34.816 --> 04:36.401
and don't worry about mine.

04:37.819 --> 04:39.112
Can't you let me feel grand for once?

04:40.697 --> 04:43.741
I felt grand all night
thinking about chipping in.

04:44.951 --> 04:47.036
Don't stomp on my grandeur.

04:48.121 --> 04:49.414
Don't send it.

04:51.499 --> 04:52.709
We might not even find her!

04:52.792 --> 04:54.794
Of course, we'll find her!

04:55.545 --> 04:57.880
If we can't find her, she'll find you!

04:58.464 --> 04:59.841
Don't you think she wants to see her dad?

05:33.374 --> 05:34.625
Are you meeting someone?

05:38.880 --> 05:39.714
I'll get going now.

05:39.797 --> 05:40.757
I'll come back tomorrow.

05:40.840 --> 05:42.091
All right, go on.

05:57.231 --> 05:58.816
It's cold. Why didn't you wait inside?

06:00.359 --> 06:01.569
I just got here.

06:02.195 --> 06:03.362
You always say that.

06:05.865 --> 06:07.033
Your nose is red.

06:09.327 --> 06:10.578
I really did just get here.

06:15.208 --> 06:16.584
Now that Noh Kang-sik is on board,

06:17.210 --> 06:19.378
I'm worried it might be too successful.

06:19.462 --> 06:21.964
How will I handle everyone's envy

06:22.048 --> 06:23.174
and jealousy?

06:23.758 --> 06:26.719
Park Gyeong-se is probably
seething with envy right now.

06:26.803 --> 06:28.638
What do I even do when I see his face?

06:29.388 --> 06:30.389
Also,

06:30.473 --> 06:34.811
what if I become so successful
that I suddenly lose my "nobody" charm?

06:36.270 --> 06:39.440
I'm scatterbrained and all over the place,
but I'm not unhappy.

06:40.108 --> 06:42.360
This is my identity and charm.

06:42.443 --> 06:43.820
If I become too successful,

06:43.903 --> 06:46.823
I'm afraid I'll suddenly lose my charm.

06:47.698 --> 06:49.117
You know what I mean.

06:49.200 --> 06:52.662
It's like a character
who starts out as a charming troublemaker

06:52.745 --> 06:56.541
but becomes serious and dull
toward the end.

06:56.624 --> 06:58.584
I'm afraid I'll end up dull like that.

06:58.668 --> 07:01.379
Isn't it weird
how all successful people are dull?

07:02.380 --> 07:04.257
Of all the pointless worries
I've heard so far,

07:04.340 --> 07:05.800
this is the most pointless one.

07:06.384 --> 07:07.343
Right?

07:08.302 --> 07:12.723
Even if I succeed,
I'll still be a scatterbrained, crazy guy

07:12.807 --> 07:13.850
who's all over the place.

07:18.980 --> 07:20.398
I'm going to be successful too.

07:21.065 --> 07:22.316
Will I lose my charm as well?

07:27.196 --> 07:28.990
Wait. Are you saying I'll lose it?

07:29.574 --> 07:31.325
I wouldn't say you'll lose it.

07:31.409 --> 07:32.952
-It's just…
-It's just what?

07:34.162 --> 07:35.746
You'll become less approachable.

07:35.830 --> 07:37.957
It's difficult enough
to approach you right now.

07:38.040 --> 07:40.543
Oh, I don't mean
you're uncomfortable to be around.

07:40.626 --> 07:42.170
It's like

07:42.253 --> 07:45.465
you're on a completely
different level from me.

07:46.841 --> 07:49.886
I still remember how shocked I was
the first time I saw you.

07:50.470 --> 07:53.347
It was like seeing an ideal face
sent from heaven.

07:54.765 --> 07:57.143
"Let this be called a face."

07:57.226 --> 07:58.936
"This is a face,

07:59.020 --> 08:01.856
so let all faces resemble it."

08:03.900 --> 08:06.319
They can resemble it,
but they can never be the same.

08:07.361 --> 08:09.572
The moment they become the same,
it's no longer ideal.

08:09.655 --> 08:11.908
An ideal is something
you can never fully achieve.

08:12.492 --> 08:14.035
That's what it means, right?

08:15.077 --> 08:16.537
That's the kind of face I saw.

08:17.163 --> 08:18.623
It feels like a miracle

08:18.706 --> 08:21.334
sitting here talking to you
when you once felt unapproachable.

08:21.918 --> 08:23.127
On top of that, you write well.

08:24.170 --> 08:25.838
Can you stop being so perfect?

08:26.756 --> 08:28.424
You almost feel unreal.

08:31.302 --> 08:32.720
Are you worshipping me?

08:34.305 --> 08:36.432
You're an ideal sent down by the gods,

08:36.516 --> 08:38.059
so of course, you deserve worship.

08:45.399 --> 08:46.776
You know your share is included

08:46.859 --> 08:48.486
in the money I received, right?

08:50.363 --> 08:52.490
Tell me whatever it is you want.

08:52.573 --> 08:53.533
Don't say "nothing."

08:54.492 --> 08:55.451
Or "anything."

08:56.577 --> 08:58.204
If I buy whatever I please,

08:58.287 --> 09:00.498
you might end up with something bizarre.

09:00.581 --> 09:02.583
I want to receive a bizarre gift.

09:02.667 --> 09:04.460
Oh, no, no, no.

09:06.254 --> 09:08.339
Stop being all lovey-dovey
and hurry up already!

09:08.422 --> 09:10.174
-Jeez.
-Hi!

09:10.800 --> 09:11.968
-Hello.
-Hey.

09:12.051 --> 09:13.553
I'm freezing.

09:13.636 --> 09:14.637
What are we having?

09:14.720 --> 09:18.224
Let's have something fancy
with green stuff sprinkled on top.

09:18.307 --> 09:19.475
I don't like food like that.

09:19.559 --> 09:21.102
They say women like that kind of food.

09:21.185 --> 09:22.436
How much are you spending?

09:23.271 --> 09:24.313
How much should I spend?

09:25.398 --> 09:26.566
-I know a place. Let's go.
-What?

09:26.649 --> 09:28.067
Don't worry. It's not expensive.

09:28.818 --> 09:32.238
By the way, are you heading
to the police station or something?

09:32.321 --> 09:34.865
I probably will soon.

09:34.949 --> 09:36.158
I'm trying out the outfit in advance.

09:36.242 --> 09:37.076
Police-station vibe.

09:37.702 --> 09:38.536
Police-station look.

09:38.619 --> 09:40.663
We could've gone somewhere more expensive!

09:40.746 --> 09:43.165
-It's expensive here!
-Hello.

09:43.249 --> 09:44.625
-Hey, nachos!
-Thank you.

09:44.709 --> 09:45.835
Enjoy.

09:53.467 --> 09:54.885
Hi, Mom.

09:54.969 --> 09:55.803
Yeah.

09:56.971 --> 09:58.598
Grandma gets discharged next week.

10:00.641 --> 10:01.934
She's okay.

10:02.018 --> 10:03.352
She can walk a bit now.

10:04.312 --> 10:07.273
Mom, I'm out right now,
so I'll call you when I get home.

10:07.857 --> 10:08.691
Bye.

10:10.359 --> 10:13.112
I thought you said
you were on bad terms with your mom.

10:13.738 --> 10:14.989
She's my stepmom.

10:16.741 --> 10:18.117
You have a stepmom too?

10:19.535 --> 10:20.911
Then what about your grandmother?

10:20.995 --> 10:22.079
She's my stepmom's mom.

10:23.289 --> 10:24.332
Then what about your dad?

10:25.333 --> 10:26.334
He passed away.

10:28.002 --> 10:29.170
When did he pass away?

10:30.004 --> 10:31.088
When I was in the 8th grade.

10:33.382 --> 10:36.052
Have the three of you
lived together ever since?

10:36.636 --> 10:37.470
Yes.

10:38.387 --> 10:40.765
My stepmom is mostly in Japan for work.

10:43.351 --> 10:44.977
They sound like good people.

10:45.061 --> 10:46.062
And you're a good person too.

10:46.937 --> 10:50.274
You see, a relationship doesn't last
if only one side is good.

10:50.358 --> 10:51.400
I get it.

10:52.026 --> 10:54.695
Even in a newly formed family,
you don't become strangers overnight

10:54.779 --> 10:55.905
just because a connection is lost.

10:55.988 --> 10:57.698
You shared a life, after all.

10:58.699 --> 11:01.285
Oh Jeong-hui and I
lost our connection a long time ago.

11:02.244 --> 11:03.162
And my dad…

11:04.747 --> 11:06.499
has a lot of problems.

11:09.251 --> 11:12.797
This mother-daughter relationship
might end at any moment now.

11:16.300 --> 11:17.134
There's a chance

11:18.052 --> 11:18.928
my name…

11:20.429 --> 11:22.139
will be all over the internet.

11:23.599 --> 11:24.975
I just hope I don't get too scared.

11:28.270 --> 11:29.105
All right.

11:29.772 --> 11:32.358
I'll take on
all the misfortune in the world,

11:32.441 --> 11:33.859
so make it big, okay?

11:33.943 --> 11:35.152
All of you make it big, okay?

11:35.236 --> 11:36.529
Hwang Dong-man.

11:36.612 --> 11:37.446
Byeon Eun-a.

11:37.530 --> 11:38.572
Lee Jun-hwan.

11:39.281 --> 11:41.075
Everyone, make it big!

11:41.158 --> 11:43.828
-Make it big!
-Make it big!

11:43.911 --> 11:45.704
-Oh, come on!
-Don't lie!

11:46.622 --> 11:48.958
Come on, you're exaggerating!

11:49.625 --> 11:51.669
Jeez, they're laughing so damn loud.

11:51.752 --> 11:52.711
Be quiet.

11:52.795 --> 11:54.463
We can't be outdone!

11:54.547 --> 11:55.840
-One, two, three!
-Two, three!

12:06.350 --> 12:08.936
The name of a target appeared, but…

12:09.019 --> 12:09.854
NATIONAL STRESS MANAGEMENT DEPARTMENT

12:16.360 --> 12:18.529
It's the country's
most notorious nutcase politician

12:19.864 --> 12:22.783
who's raising everyone's blood pressure
and must be taken out quickly.

12:24.118 --> 12:24.952
But…

12:26.203 --> 12:27.288
it's his wife.

12:35.045 --> 12:37.715
She might be a nutcase,
but she's still his wife.

12:37.798 --> 12:39.425
He can't just let her die, can he?

12:45.848 --> 12:46.891
But then

12:47.475 --> 12:51.270
she says the one line
that really pisses off the protagonist

12:51.353 --> 12:55.441
and makes him say, "Screw it. Just die."

12:55.524 --> 12:56.650
What could it be?

13:00.446 --> 13:02.031
What could it be?

13:04.492 --> 13:05.451
What did you say?

13:07.119 --> 13:08.204
When will the script be ready?

13:08.287 --> 13:09.622
When will the script be ready?

13:11.790 --> 13:14.793
We were supposed to give them
episodes three and four ages ago.

13:25.054 --> 13:27.056
Stop struggling with them.

13:27.139 --> 13:29.016
Just hand them over and get it over with.

13:30.768 --> 13:32.478
I could think of so many moments

13:32.561 --> 13:34.396
that would piss off the protagonist
if he were a writer.

13:34.480 --> 13:37.024
Why did I make him
a Grade 9 civil servant?

13:37.107 --> 13:37.942
Say what?

13:40.152 --> 13:41.946
His friend gets flagged as a target.

13:43.989 --> 13:46.617
All of the memories
and history they shared

13:46.700 --> 13:48.827
flash before his eyes.

13:50.162 --> 13:52.248
He gets choked up. He can't stand it.

13:52.331 --> 13:53.707
He's trying to save them,

13:53.791 --> 13:55.251
but then they ask,

13:56.001 --> 13:58.003
"When will the script be ready?"

13:58.629 --> 14:00.464
"What the… What did you just say?"

14:00.548 --> 14:01.715
"'When will the script be ready?'"

14:02.466 --> 14:06.095
He told them not to say that one thing,
but they said it anyway.

14:06.178 --> 14:08.097
He tells them,
"I'm talking to you right now,

14:08.180 --> 14:10.432
but 99% of my brain
is focused on the script."

14:10.516 --> 14:13.352
"I'm running on the last 1% of my brain,

14:14.520 --> 14:18.190
doing everything I can to keep you alive,

14:18.274 --> 14:19.400
but it's no use."

14:20.484 --> 14:22.403
"Just go."

14:24.280 --> 14:25.447
"Take care."

14:25.531 --> 14:26.365
"I can't see you off."

14:35.374 --> 14:38.002
There are so many moments

14:38.085 --> 14:40.796
when writers get so pissed off
that they just give up.

14:41.297 --> 14:44.300
I just thought of a rage trigger
for the protagonist!

14:48.012 --> 14:49.513
"You only make two million won a month?"

14:53.726 --> 14:54.560
That's it.

14:56.812 --> 14:58.606
"You only make two million won a month?"

14:58.689 --> 15:01.525
That's it. You're a genius, Writer Park.

15:01.609 --> 15:02.818
You figured it out.

15:02.902 --> 15:03.736
You're a genius.

15:03.819 --> 15:05.195
This is it.

15:05.279 --> 15:08.073
"You only make two million won a month?"

15:09.033 --> 15:10.951
"The protagonist is filled with rage

15:11.035 --> 15:12.786
and finally comes to a decision."

15:12.870 --> 15:14.914
-Bang!
-Bang! And they're dead.

15:14.997 --> 15:17.416
He fires nonstop. All right.

15:17.499 --> 15:18.792
Hold on. Let's think here.

15:18.876 --> 15:21.378
"The protagonist starts shooting
to an excessive degree."

15:21.462 --> 15:23.547
"You only make two million won a month?"

15:23.631 --> 15:24.757
"Only two million won a month?"

15:27.551 --> 15:29.803
"There's no point in drawing this out…"

15:30.471 --> 15:32.556
Make it big, Hwang Dong-man!

15:33.515 --> 15:34.558
Thank you.

15:34.642 --> 15:38.228
-Make it big!
-Thank you! I'll do my best!

15:38.312 --> 15:39.563
Make it big, Eun-a.

15:40.314 --> 15:42.858
-Make it big.
-Everyone, make it big.

15:45.945 --> 15:47.071
Let's go!

15:48.155 --> 15:49.323
Where are we going?

15:49.949 --> 15:51.158
-Where is she going?
-Where?

15:51.241 --> 15:53.118
Where are we going?

15:56.872 --> 15:58.916
Mi-ran!

15:59.500 --> 16:01.210
No! Don't do this, Mi-ran.

16:01.293 --> 16:02.878
-Why not?
-Please don't.

16:02.962 --> 16:04.380
He'll beat me to death.

16:04.463 --> 16:05.798
Okay, okay.

16:05.881 --> 16:06.715
Let's leave.

16:10.052 --> 16:10.886
Don't!

16:10.970 --> 16:12.096
Hwang Dong-man!

16:27.194 --> 16:28.862
She went in!

16:31.573 --> 16:33.117
What do we do?

16:53.679 --> 16:54.722
Just as I expected,

16:56.223 --> 16:57.725
you've been drinking.

17:01.562 --> 17:04.231
I had a drink myself.

17:06.191 --> 17:10.612
There was no other way for me to wipe away

17:12.114 --> 17:14.033
the wrong that remains somewhere.

17:23.000 --> 17:24.585
I stopped by because I wanted to see you.

17:44.605 --> 17:45.564
She's back.

17:51.779 --> 17:53.781
This is why I told you not to go in.

17:58.118 --> 17:59.411
Just you wait!

18:00.704 --> 18:02.372
You'll be into me before you know it.

18:10.547 --> 18:11.965
Wait for me!

18:13.175 --> 18:15.844
The ball goes to the goalkeeper,
Choi Chun-ho.

18:17.221 --> 18:18.097
It got cut off.

18:18.180 --> 18:20.015
Yes, the pass came up short.

18:21.141 --> 18:22.142
But the pressure continues.

18:23.977 --> 18:27.147
If you file a lawsuit
and the media gets hold of this,

18:27.231 --> 18:29.024
it's a given that both sides
will get screwed.

18:29.108 --> 18:32.111
I don't care if we both get screwed.

18:32.903 --> 18:33.946
It's not just you two.

18:34.613 --> 18:37.199
-What about Jung Hyeon-u?
-He has nothing to do with this!

18:37.282 --> 18:38.784
It was a fight between Jang Mi-ran and me.

18:38.867 --> 18:41.328
You think she'll stay quiet
about why you guys fought?

18:41.411 --> 18:42.996
She'll disclose every last detail.

18:45.332 --> 18:47.459
Jang Mi-ran was 100% at fault
for what she did.

18:47.543 --> 18:49.503
We'll make her apologize,

18:50.504 --> 18:52.131
so let's settle this for 100 million won.

18:52.214 --> 18:53.257
SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT

18:55.843 --> 18:57.302
You think I'm doing this for money?

18:57.386 --> 18:58.428
You know what?

18:59.346 --> 19:02.391
Even if I killed her,
it still wouldn't be enough!

19:02.474 --> 19:04.601
Even if it means humiliating myself

19:04.685 --> 19:06.937
by admitting
I got beaten up like an idiot,

19:07.020 --> 19:08.981
I'm going to take Jang Mi-ran down
for good.

19:09.606 --> 19:11.775
I'll never accept a payoff

19:13.193 --> 19:14.361
and pretend it never happened.

19:17.072 --> 19:18.907
Why aren't you saying anything?

19:19.741 --> 19:22.578
Of course, we'll file a lawsuit, but…

19:24.705 --> 19:27.082
Let's do it a bit later.

19:27.166 --> 19:29.001
My drama is out right now,

19:29.084 --> 19:30.919
and I'm going to Taiwan next week
to promote it.

19:37.301 --> 19:39.344
Jung Hyeon-u is a fool.

19:40.012 --> 19:43.056
He should've insisted on
going after Jang Mi-ran.

19:44.725 --> 19:46.435
This makes things difficult.

19:50.063 --> 19:53.025
What makes a woman
grab another woman by their hair?

19:54.026 --> 19:56.653
I've seen it in dramas
but never in real life.

19:57.362 --> 19:58.488
I regret it too.

19:59.114 --> 20:00.490
Grabbing her hair was lame.

20:01.325 --> 20:03.827
Next time,
I'll hit her with a roundhouse kick.

20:03.911 --> 20:05.621
Don't be so stubborn.

20:06.663 --> 20:08.665
You may never get to act again.

20:09.374 --> 20:10.542
You know,

20:11.168 --> 20:12.794
I just want it all out in the open.

20:12.878 --> 20:16.131
I want everything revealed
about how this whole mess started

20:16.215 --> 20:18.634
and put it out there for the world to see.

20:19.468 --> 20:20.510
"Jung Hyeon-u…

20:22.137 --> 20:23.263
liked…

20:24.681 --> 20:25.682
Jang Mi-ran."

20:27.726 --> 20:28.644
"Jang Mi-ran…

20:30.062 --> 20:31.104
isn't…

20:32.397 --> 20:33.273
a crazy bitch."

20:40.989 --> 20:43.450
-Tell them I want to see them.
-I will.

20:44.034 --> 20:46.286
What about the Knock knock knock contract?

20:46.370 --> 20:47.496
It'll come through soon.

21:00.300 --> 21:01.551
Welcome.

21:01.635 --> 21:02.552
Come in.

21:06.306 --> 21:07.266
Take a seat.

21:10.477 --> 21:11.812
Here, try this.

21:17.317 --> 21:20.320
I wondered why you never backed down
when I was on your case

21:21.113 --> 21:23.323
and what made you act so defiant.

21:24.199 --> 21:25.492
You had an ace up your sleeve.

21:27.911 --> 21:29.329
When did you start writing?

21:30.247 --> 21:31.540
Have you written a lot?

21:34.084 --> 21:35.085
No.

21:35.794 --> 21:36.712
How many have you written?

21:37.921 --> 21:38.964
Not many.

21:40.173 --> 21:41.091
I knew it.

21:42.384 --> 21:44.052
I have a good eye for things.

21:44.761 --> 21:46.555
I called you "Ax," didn't I?

21:46.638 --> 21:48.015
Golden Ax.

21:48.724 --> 21:50.017
There was something different

21:50.100 --> 21:52.060
about the things you said
compared to other producers.

21:52.144 --> 21:55.314
There are things only someone
who's actually written can say.

21:55.397 --> 21:56.773
If you haven't written, you wouldn't know.

22:00.902 --> 22:02.195
Let's keep the fact that you're Yeong-sil

22:03.989 --> 22:04.948
just between you and me.

22:06.491 --> 22:09.828
You know that Ma Jae-yeong
desperately tried to hide you, right?

22:09.911 --> 22:13.206
And it's not like I don't know why
he tried to do so.

22:13.874 --> 22:15.751
He's already on edge as it is.

22:15.834 --> 22:18.253
Nothing good will come
from provoking the director.

22:19.629 --> 22:23.008
Knock knock knock will go under his name,
and he'll pay you.

22:23.675 --> 22:24.593
And let's sign

22:25.802 --> 22:27.304
a separate writer's contract.

22:29.598 --> 22:30.766
I'll pay you top rate.

22:33.185 --> 22:34.478
You know me.

22:35.812 --> 22:37.189
I never miss out on a sure bet.

22:39.775 --> 22:41.860
I'll only write
when I have something to write.

22:43.236 --> 22:44.488
I won't write for money.

22:46.865 --> 22:47.783
You're so cool.

22:50.327 --> 22:51.661
But you know,

22:52.621 --> 22:54.498
writing comes from
the sense of repaying a debt.

22:55.248 --> 22:57.959
You know Writer Park who wrote The Fools?

22:58.043 --> 23:00.545
After gambling away their signing fee,

23:00.629 --> 23:04.216
they couldn't pay up,
so they wrote nonstop and came up with it.

23:04.299 --> 23:05.926
It ended up being a big hit.

23:06.510 --> 23:07.886
Money makes writing happen.

23:09.262 --> 23:10.972
Without money, it doesn't happen.

23:12.891 --> 23:13.892
How about 100 million won per screenplay?

23:17.979 --> 23:19.564
Let's sign a contract for just two.

23:23.693 --> 23:26.154
You don't have to come to work,

23:26.238 --> 23:28.115
but you can if you want.

23:28.198 --> 23:29.241
Do whatever suits you.

23:32.494 --> 23:35.580
So Writer Park caused a stir overseas too.

23:35.664 --> 23:36.498
Later on,

23:37.290 --> 23:38.500
they wrote it all.

23:38.583 --> 23:41.503
Seasons two, three, and even four.

23:43.588 --> 23:44.422
Hey.

23:52.264 --> 23:53.640
The doors are closing.

23:57.602 --> 23:59.104
Are you on your way back from lunch?

23:59.688 --> 24:01.398
Yes. Looks like you are too.

24:01.481 --> 24:02.315
Yeah.

24:04.025 --> 24:06.611
The key crew is set now, right?

24:07.237 --> 24:09.489
We just need to confirm
the production designer today.

24:10.240 --> 24:11.074
I see.

24:17.330 --> 24:19.499
Why did he act like
he was hiding something?

24:21.084 --> 24:22.377
He looked flustered, right?

24:24.337 --> 24:26.715
I'm not really sure.

24:29.384 --> 24:31.469
What's the deal with them eating together?

24:32.137 --> 24:34.514
-Who?
-Mr. Choi and Byeon Eun-a.

24:34.598 --> 24:36.516
It smelled like they had barbecue.

24:37.767 --> 24:38.810
Really?

24:54.367 --> 24:55.535
ALL THE LUCK TO THE CAST AND CREW
OF VILLAIN HUNT

24:55.619 --> 24:56.953
SUPPORTING NOH KANG-SIK!
FROM HWANG DONG-MAN, KO HYE-JIN

25:02.042 --> 25:04.127
-Please enjoy!
-Thank you.

25:11.343 --> 25:12.510
They built the set well.

25:13.094 --> 25:14.304
Do a better job, you punk!

25:16.139 --> 25:17.307
Give me a break.

25:18.016 --> 25:19.226
"Give me a break"?

25:20.602 --> 25:22.896
You think I don't know what you do?

25:23.688 --> 25:26.316
You intimidate your juniors
to knock them off their game.

25:26.399 --> 25:27.234
-Hello.
-What's wrong?

25:27.317 --> 25:28.735
If your co-star does a good job,

25:28.818 --> 25:30.195
-you do whatever you can
-They got into a fight.

25:30.278 --> 25:32.572
to make sure that scene doesn't get used.

25:32.656 --> 25:34.324
Wow, Jeong-min's good at acting.

25:35.951 --> 25:36.868
He's not acting.

25:39.663 --> 25:40.497
Hey.

25:41.289 --> 25:42.123
Tell me.

25:43.792 --> 25:44.834
You think you're a good actor?

25:47.504 --> 25:48.338
Yes.

25:50.131 --> 25:52.926
Does a good actor
cut off their co-star's flow

25:53.009 --> 25:55.637
and do whatever they want?

25:55.720 --> 26:00.558
You're not confident in your acting!
That's why you're all over the place!

26:00.642 --> 26:03.103
Or maybe it's your old-school acting style

26:03.186 --> 26:07.399
that can't keep up with my range
as an actor.

26:07.482 --> 26:09.526
Are you kidding me?

26:09.609 --> 26:13.029
Let's just focus on acting, okay?

26:13.113 --> 26:13.947
Just acting,

26:14.447 --> 26:16.241
not this hierarchy bullshit.

26:17.659 --> 26:19.327
Hey, show some respect.

26:19.411 --> 26:20.245
Got it?

26:22.122 --> 26:23.123
Got it?

26:25.834 --> 26:27.794
Goddamn it.

26:27.877 --> 26:30.213
Screw this. I'm done here.

26:30.297 --> 26:32.632
Do you really fucking
expect me to shoot this

26:32.716 --> 26:34.759
while getting beaten up at my age?

26:34.843 --> 26:36.761
I'll pay whatever penalty and quit.

26:37.262 --> 26:40.765
It's disgusting how this whole industry
keeps quiet because of guys like him.

26:40.849 --> 26:43.685
I'll call every reporter I know,

26:43.768 --> 26:47.439
tell them all the crap you've pulled,
and leave this industry.

26:47.522 --> 26:50.650
Someone like you should've been
blacklisted a long time ago.

26:50.734 --> 26:51.943
You know that?

26:52.027 --> 26:53.528
Go right ahead.

26:54.154 --> 26:54.988
Do it.

26:55.071 --> 26:56.740
Go ahead and call the reporters, you punk!

26:56.823 --> 26:57.741
Call them now!

26:57.824 --> 26:58.700
Let go of me!

26:58.783 --> 27:00.076
-I said let go of me!
-Hit me.

27:00.160 --> 27:01.286
-Let go of me, you jerks!
-Hit me!

27:01.369 --> 27:02.203
-Go ahead! Hit me!
-Hey!

27:02.287 --> 27:04.164
Hey, stop, stop.

27:07.417 --> 27:08.668
Please calm down.

27:10.045 --> 27:10.879
I mean…

27:13.631 --> 27:14.632
This?

27:15.342 --> 27:17.177
How is this a hit?

27:17.761 --> 27:19.137
Who the hell are you?

27:19.721 --> 27:21.056
I'm sorry.

27:21.139 --> 27:23.141
I get that you're offended.

27:23.224 --> 27:26.353
Then why don't you
just make him feel the same way?

27:28.271 --> 27:31.066
Just do this and make him feel offended.

27:31.149 --> 27:32.817
Come on, it's not that hard to do.

27:32.901 --> 27:34.152
How is this hard?

27:34.235 --> 27:36.738
Have you lost your mind too, you punk?

27:36.821 --> 27:40.158
See? You can see on his face
that he's offended.

27:40.241 --> 27:41.326
-I'm sorry.
-I mean…

27:41.409 --> 27:43.661
-I'm sorry. Let's go.
-Wait, Hye-jin. Hold on.

27:43.745 --> 27:47.082
I don't get it. Why are you getting mad
because he offended you?

27:47.165 --> 27:49.709
You just need to offend him right back!

27:50.210 --> 27:53.296
Why would you threaten to quit
and talk to reporters

27:53.380 --> 27:54.547
over something like this?

27:54.631 --> 27:56.883
Again, who the hell are you?

27:56.966 --> 27:58.009
I'm sorry.

27:58.093 --> 27:59.094
Let's go!

27:59.177 --> 28:01.221
-I said let's go!
-I heard you!

28:01.304 --> 28:04.474
Call the reporters,
but at least wait until after my film!

28:04.557 --> 28:06.559
Wait until I'm done with my film!

28:07.227 --> 28:08.812
Come on, don't you agree?

28:08.895 --> 28:11.689
Do you know how hard I worked
to get to this point?

28:12.273 --> 28:13.358
That's enough, you bastard!

28:13.441 --> 28:14.651
I ought to just…

28:17.404 --> 28:18.238
You know what?

28:18.780 --> 28:20.573
-I'm not offended.
-For goodness' sake.

28:20.657 --> 28:22.283
What's there to get offended about?

28:41.386 --> 28:42.762
When I tell people

28:44.180 --> 28:46.057
that Hwang Dong-man is the director

28:46.141 --> 28:47.976
and the lead actor is Noh Kang-sik,

28:48.560 --> 28:49.853
everyone says the same thing.

28:50.395 --> 28:51.896
"Oh no, Ms. Ko."

28:52.647 --> 28:54.566
"That'll take years off your life."

28:56.484 --> 28:58.945
I refuse to work myself into anything
that leads to cancer.

29:01.114 --> 29:02.198
Remember what I said?

29:03.533 --> 29:05.034
I plan to live to 100.

29:06.578 --> 29:09.122
If I think it might give me cancer,
I'll scrap it immediately.

29:10.957 --> 29:13.668
So just shut up and stay still!

29:13.752 --> 29:15.837
Don't do anything or say anything!

29:15.920 --> 29:17.464
And don't step in.

29:17.547 --> 29:19.507
Nothing improves when you step in!

29:20.341 --> 29:22.594
Just say, "Ready, action, cut." Okay?

29:24.220 --> 29:25.054
Okay.

29:35.940 --> 29:40.278
Why did you and Mr. Choi
have lunch together out of nowhere?

29:41.154 --> 29:42.572
Did you tell him you're quitting?

29:43.531 --> 29:46.618
He goes hard on people, but the second
someone says they're quitting,

29:46.701 --> 29:48.286
he softens up
and tries to talk them out of it.

29:50.371 --> 29:51.956
What did you two talk about?

29:53.541 --> 29:54.793
Why do you want to know?

29:56.169 --> 29:58.505
Are you anxious
that he's doting on me again?

29:58.588 --> 30:00.340
Watch your mouth, will you?

30:01.382 --> 30:02.383
I'm your senior.

30:02.467 --> 30:03.301
So what?

30:03.927 --> 30:05.053
You can talk to me however you want?

30:05.136 --> 30:07.639
You could've just said
that you somehow ended up eating together.

30:07.722 --> 30:12.060
The way you asked me didn't allow for
such a casual response.

30:12.811 --> 30:13.645
You were being snide.

30:19.943 --> 30:21.694
I won't let her get away with this.

30:22.195 --> 30:24.948
Why does Mr. Choi listen to that brat?

30:25.615 --> 30:28.451
She's against changing the protagonist
of Knock knock knock to a woman?

30:28.535 --> 30:30.203
Who does she think she is?

30:30.286 --> 30:34.165
Even the director approved it,
so who the hell is she to object?

30:35.083 --> 30:36.459
Goddamn it.

30:49.639 --> 30:52.100
You've made a lot of progress
in developing it.

30:53.810 --> 30:55.353
Yes, I did.

30:56.271 --> 30:58.022
Let's put a hold on
Jang Mi-ran's contract.

30:59.065 --> 30:59.899
Why all of a sudden?

31:00.483 --> 31:02.610
This is under wraps
because of her current drama,

31:02.694 --> 31:04.654
but something big is about to drop.

31:04.737 --> 31:05.780
What is it?

31:05.864 --> 31:08.074
A criminal lawsuit.

31:08.157 --> 31:08.992
For assault.

31:09.868 --> 31:12.537
I don't think we can cast
Oh Jeong-hui either.

31:12.620 --> 31:13.705
Damn it.

31:15.290 --> 31:16.791
And we don't have Noh Kang-sik.

31:17.625 --> 31:20.003
We can't do Knock knock knock
without Oh Jeong-hui.

31:21.629 --> 31:23.089
Put a hold on her contract for now.

31:24.340 --> 31:25.425
MS. OH JEONG-HUI

31:25.508 --> 31:26.593
This is a mess.

31:27.468 --> 31:28.887
Hello, Ms. Oh!

31:29.721 --> 31:30.597
Right, yes.

31:31.806 --> 31:33.808
Goodness, we're not stalling.

31:33.892 --> 31:35.894
Of course, we want you.

31:35.977 --> 31:36.811
Absolutely.

31:37.687 --> 31:39.105
It's nothing major,

31:40.440 --> 31:43.401
but there's been some talk
about changing the protagonist to a woman

31:43.484 --> 31:45.236
since it'll shift the mood entirely.

31:46.738 --> 31:47.697
The writer did.

31:48.948 --> 31:49.866
Yes, Yeong-sil.

31:49.949 --> 31:53.578
We can't completely ignore
what the writer says.

32:02.921 --> 32:05.632
The moment Hyo-jin opens her mouth,

32:05.715 --> 32:07.717
I'm bored to death.

32:10.053 --> 32:12.013
Every single word is boring.

32:13.222 --> 32:14.641
She seems like someone

32:15.934 --> 32:17.685
who'll never open up,
no matter how long you know her.

32:17.769 --> 32:20.563
She's not someone
who intentionally hides what's inside…

32:22.774 --> 32:25.276
but someone who doesn't know
how to communicate what's inside.

32:27.320 --> 32:29.656
How can a person like that
be in filmmaking?

32:31.366 --> 32:34.285
I'm in The Eight Club with her,

32:34.994 --> 32:38.498
but I've only talked to her
for maybe ten minutes at most.

32:39.707 --> 32:42.043
-It's awkward when I'm alone with her.
-Right?

32:42.126 --> 32:42.961
Yes.

32:43.044 --> 32:45.213
When she starts talking,

32:46.464 --> 32:49.592
I hate the thought of the sound
of her voice touching me in any way,

32:49.676 --> 32:52.303
-so my body just stiffens up.
-Right.

32:52.387 --> 32:53.805
-And I can't hear anything.
-Right.

32:53.888 --> 32:56.140
-It's like my ears automatically shut off.
-I hate it.

32:56.724 --> 32:58.434
But when I talk to you,

32:59.519 --> 33:01.229
it feels like we have a real conversation.

33:03.815 --> 33:05.149
I'm so moved.

33:06.275 --> 33:09.028
People always say I talk nonstop
and that I can't hold a conversation.

33:09.612 --> 33:10.822
You do talk nonstop.

33:12.073 --> 33:13.408
Right.

33:13.491 --> 33:16.327
When we meet,
you do 80% of the talking on your own.

33:16.411 --> 33:17.954
Right, on my own.

33:18.788 --> 33:20.373
But it's never boring.

33:21.290 --> 33:22.750
Everything you say really hits me.

33:23.334 --> 33:24.961
And my ears open up.

33:25.044 --> 33:27.672
Sometimes, it's to the point
where I want to take notes.

33:30.717 --> 33:33.219
I had planned
to keep my mouth shut for a while

33:34.137 --> 33:35.346
because I got really chewed out today.

33:35.430 --> 33:37.640
No, don't keep your mouth shut.

33:37.724 --> 33:39.892
Yes, ma'am! I won't keep my mouth shut!

33:39.976 --> 33:41.519
At least, not in front of you.

33:47.567 --> 33:49.819
I feel like I can finally breathe
when I talk to you.

33:50.820 --> 33:53.823
It feels like everything you say
is what I would say,

33:54.449 --> 33:57.702
and you always seem to understand
exactly what I mean.

34:02.290 --> 34:04.167
I'd always get nervous

34:06.127 --> 34:07.712
when talking to people.

34:11.466 --> 34:13.051
I'd wonder,
"How are they taking what I'm saying?"

34:20.725 --> 34:22.560
But when I'm with you,

34:23.478 --> 34:27.231
it feels like my heart bursts open
and everything flows out smoothly

34:28.316 --> 34:30.276
without any hesitation.

34:32.028 --> 34:33.654
I feel the same.

34:34.781 --> 34:36.240
Everything you say
feels like what I would say.

34:39.035 --> 34:41.454
Do you think
we were meant to be one person,

34:42.080 --> 34:44.707
but got split into two
and came into the world?

34:45.666 --> 34:48.544
I would've liked you
even if you were a man,

34:49.295 --> 34:51.172
or even if you were a tree.

34:51.255 --> 34:53.800
And if you were the wind,
I would've been nuts about you.

34:56.094 --> 34:56.969
Eun-a,

34:57.762 --> 34:59.806
you're too precious to be held

35:00.431 --> 35:03.601
within such a small frame
and a confined space.

35:04.310 --> 35:05.436
I want the whole world

35:05.978 --> 35:07.480
to be Byeon Eun-a.

35:11.109 --> 35:12.026
It's Byeon Eun-a.

35:13.694 --> 35:14.529
It's Byeon Eun-a.

35:15.488 --> 35:16.405
It's Byeon Eun-a.

35:19.784 --> 35:20.618
Eun-a?

35:21.494 --> 35:23.412
Why did you get so small?

35:23.496 --> 35:24.705
Oh dear.

35:25.998 --> 35:27.625
Please take good care of Eun-a.

35:29.544 --> 35:32.088
Oh, Eun-a! Oh no! Eun-a!

35:34.173 --> 35:35.133
Eun-a…

35:44.433 --> 35:46.018
You know,

35:46.644 --> 35:48.396
you give off a teenage boy vibe.

35:51.524 --> 35:52.441
Is that a compliment?

35:53.025 --> 35:54.026
A huge one.

35:55.903 --> 35:57.029
Eun-a.

35:58.114 --> 35:59.532
-Eun-a.
-Eun-a.

36:03.244 --> 36:04.954
Welcome.

36:12.461 --> 36:14.213
Just a second. I'll bring more drinks.

36:17.592 --> 36:18.718
Oh, hello.

36:18.801 --> 36:20.303
-It's been a while.
-Yes, it has.

36:21.262 --> 36:22.847
I hear you're debuting soon?

36:25.016 --> 36:29.020
I've actually been meaning to tell you.

36:29.103 --> 36:30.605
After all, you're the reason I'm here,

36:31.189 --> 36:33.983
and you taught me how to write.

36:34.650 --> 36:38.112
So I really wanted to tell you
that I was debuting.

36:38.196 --> 36:39.363
Thank you!

36:41.782 --> 36:45.578
I worked with Ms. Oh for a bit
a long time ago.

36:45.661 --> 36:46.913
It was

36:46.996 --> 36:49.999
a very embarrassing memory,
so I don't usually talk about it.

36:50.082 --> 36:52.084
I worked on the directing team
for Dogs and Cats.

36:52.668 --> 36:55.588
Oh, this is Producer Byeon Eun-a
from Choi Film.

36:55.671 --> 36:56.505
Let me introduce…

36:56.589 --> 36:57.590
Sit down.

36:58.507 --> 37:00.009
Right, let's sit down.

37:01.385 --> 37:03.095
-Would you like a drink--
-No, thank you.

37:06.432 --> 37:09.769
I heard the writer of Knock knock knock
is against casting me in the role.

37:10.645 --> 37:12.772
I'd like to know why you're against it,

37:13.522 --> 37:14.607
Ms. Yeong-sil.

37:18.903 --> 37:21.447
Are you against
changing the protagonist to a woman,

37:22.114 --> 37:24.492
or are you against me playing the role?

37:26.369 --> 37:28.996
Just give it to me straight.
That's why I'm here.

37:35.253 --> 37:36.170
She wouldn't be

37:36.837 --> 37:37.922
against it.

37:39.215 --> 37:40.132
Right?

37:44.845 --> 37:47.223
Which is scarier?
A crazy woman or a crazy man?

37:48.266 --> 37:52.270
Between a crazy woman and a crazy man
roaming the streets,

37:53.020 --> 37:54.272
which is scarier?

37:55.481 --> 37:58.150
Wouldn't a strong man who could harm me…

38:00.444 --> 38:01.862
be scarier?

38:02.655 --> 38:05.950
Which is scarier?
A female ghost or a male ghost?

38:06.575 --> 38:07.576
Fear…

38:09.328 --> 38:11.038
is an emotional state,

38:11.122 --> 38:12.164
not a physical one.

38:13.124 --> 38:14.875
If strong men are scary,

38:14.959 --> 38:18.045
are all horror film protagonists
supposed to be men?

38:18.796 --> 38:21.549
I thought you were savvy,
but you're surprisingly narrow-minded.

38:22.883 --> 38:25.970
Your objection to changing
to a female protagonist isn't valid.

38:28.264 --> 38:30.349
Is there a personal reason
you object to casting me?

38:37.648 --> 38:38.733
Because it's sickening.

38:43.529 --> 38:45.448
That disgusting ambition of yours

38:46.824 --> 38:48.117
that knows no limits

38:49.452 --> 38:50.703
and keeps pushing its way in.

38:53.331 --> 38:55.666
I want you to know
you can't have everything.

38:56.834 --> 38:58.210
No matter how good they act,

38:58.711 --> 39:01.839
the actor's own emotions
still come through.

39:03.716 --> 39:04.884
It's always a battle.

39:06.802 --> 39:07.803
You have to outshine others.

39:07.887 --> 39:09.680
It's always more, more, more.

39:12.308 --> 39:15.269
Have you ever acted in a supporting role?

39:16.562 --> 39:18.314
Have you ever once enjoyed working?

39:19.231 --> 39:21.650
Enjoy working? Do I look like an amateur?

39:25.571 --> 39:28.032
I believe Daniel Day-Lewis
worked as a shoemaker.

39:29.200 --> 39:31.494
You have to reach the end
to know there's nothing special

39:31.577 --> 39:32.661
before you take a different path.

39:33.245 --> 39:34.497
Don't tell me to become a shoemaker

39:34.580 --> 39:36.582
when I haven't even reached
the end of my path yet.

39:37.166 --> 39:41.420
If someone says money isn't a big deal,
do you agree and give in?

39:42.004 --> 39:45.341
It's not too late to make money
and come to that decision on your own.

39:46.133 --> 39:47.259
It's the same thing.

39:47.343 --> 39:49.095
You have to reach the end of hell to know.

40:05.694 --> 40:07.071
Do you even know what hell is?

40:16.872 --> 40:19.291
You can go through hell
at just nine years old.

40:21.877 --> 40:24.171
I don't know.
It's taboo to talk about her.

40:24.255 --> 40:25.923
Oh, I know her name.

40:26.006 --> 40:27.216
It's Byeon Si-on.

40:27.299 --> 40:29.260
Which sounds better,
Byeon Si-on or Byeon Eun-a?

40:39.186 --> 40:41.272
It's not true. Right, Eun-a?

40:43.816 --> 40:47.653
Take a look at every line you've written
and your desire to kill in each one.

40:48.279 --> 40:51.240
Your motivation is fueled
by your hatred for me.

40:52.825 --> 40:56.162
They say you can't blame parents
once you turn 40.

40:56.245 --> 40:58.247
What will you use as motivation then?

41:00.708 --> 41:02.418
How's your grandmother doing?

41:06.422 --> 41:11.010
Anyone who absolutely detests something
also has something they absolutely love.

41:11.093 --> 41:12.094
It's how they live on.

41:24.815 --> 41:27.318
As soon as I was born,
I was abandoned every day.

41:28.402 --> 41:29.862
Your deep sigh,

41:29.945 --> 41:31.489
your look…

41:33.949 --> 41:35.326
Even if it kills me…

41:37.828 --> 41:40.748
I want to show you how wrong you were.

41:40.831 --> 41:43.083
Just write it all down and give it to me.

41:43.167 --> 41:46.378
Write down everything you remember
about how much of a bitch I was.

41:46.962 --> 41:49.798
You can write a hundred pages
or a thousand, and I'll read it.

41:49.882 --> 41:53.802
I'll read it every day
like it's a daily Bible verse.

41:53.886 --> 41:56.180
I'll repent while reading it.

41:57.014 --> 41:59.808
I'll spend the rest of my life

41:59.892 --> 42:02.478
dwelling on that precious wound
you can't seem to let go!

42:02.561 --> 42:03.395
So you just write it down

42:04.021 --> 42:05.314
and be done with it!

42:08.400 --> 42:10.945
Some writers keep reliving their own pain.

42:11.862 --> 42:14.323
You used all of your hatred for me
in writing Knock knock knock.

42:14.406 --> 42:16.200
There's nothing left to write about it,

42:16.283 --> 42:17.952
so just let it go and move on!

42:19.286 --> 42:22.706
Stop rehashing the same emotions
and letting your writing get rusty!

42:28.128 --> 42:29.505
The next round will reveal

42:30.297 --> 42:32.174
what kind of writing Ma Jae-yeong produces

42:32.258 --> 42:34.176
and what kind of writing
Yeong-sil produces.

42:35.469 --> 42:39.139
It'll determine who Knock knock knock
originally belonged to.

43:22.349 --> 43:24.977
You used all of your hatred for me
in writing Knock knock knock.

43:25.060 --> 43:26.687
There's nothing left to write about it,

43:26.770 --> 43:28.606
so just let it go and move on!

43:29.481 --> 43:33.485
If you could erase your childhood memories
to escape from this pain,

43:34.153 --> 43:35.029
would you do it?

43:37.406 --> 43:38.407
No.

43:41.827 --> 43:43.954
Without this pain, that woman…

43:45.539 --> 43:47.541
would be completely innocent.

43:59.845 --> 44:03.432
She was neglected
and grew up without her parents.

44:03.974 --> 44:05.643
I didn't think much of it at the time,

44:05.726 --> 44:08.687
but looking back now,
my heart simply goes out to her.

44:09.688 --> 44:11.106
I wonder what she's doing now

44:11.857 --> 44:13.275
and how her life is going.

44:14.693 --> 44:17.488
That sloppy gimbap

44:17.571 --> 44:19.406
she clearly made herself.

44:20.324 --> 44:22.117
I still think about that sad gimbap

44:22.910 --> 44:25.287
and how she forced it down.

44:30.709 --> 44:31.543
NO WAY, LOOK AT THIS

44:31.627 --> 44:32.670
POOR THING… THE KID DIDN'T DESERVE THIS

44:36.131 --> 44:37.341
Has it ever occurred to you

44:37.424 --> 44:39.259
that it might be rude
to post something like this?

44:40.052 --> 44:42.680
This child is now an adult.

44:42.763 --> 44:44.973
How would she feel reading this?

44:48.894 --> 44:52.981
What about the pain
of having to relive a childhood

44:54.233 --> 44:56.443
that everyone remembers as pitiful?

44:57.653 --> 44:59.363
You may act sympathetic,

44:59.988 --> 45:01.115
but right now,

45:01.865 --> 45:05.786
you're keeping her trapped
in that painful past and toying with her.

45:07.037 --> 45:08.872
Please don't pretend it's compassion.

45:09.540 --> 45:11.667
Don't pretend it's compassion,
you assholes.

45:27.433 --> 45:31.186
NATIONAL STRESS MANAGEMENT DEPARTMENT
EPISODE 4

45:31.270 --> 45:34.440
BY PARK GYEONG-SE, PARK JEONG-MIN

45:54.376 --> 45:56.503
-Hey.
-Did you read the script?

45:57.379 --> 45:58.505
Yeah.

45:59.131 --> 46:00.048
What do you think?

46:01.258 --> 46:02.259
It's fun.

46:03.051 --> 46:03.969
That's it?

46:04.052 --> 46:04.928
What else should I say?

46:05.512 --> 46:06.805
Is it really fun?

46:07.473 --> 46:08.515
Yeah, it is.

46:08.599 --> 46:10.350
Then why are you talking like that?

46:10.434 --> 46:11.977
How should I be talking?

46:13.520 --> 46:15.105
I say it's fun, and you still complain.

46:16.231 --> 46:18.066
Are you attending
Director Lee's premiere later?

46:19.401 --> 46:21.028
No, I want to sleep.

46:21.111 --> 46:22.696
Come to the after-party, then.

46:22.779 --> 46:23.906
Forget it. I'm sleeping.

46:24.907 --> 46:25.741
Bye.

46:49.806 --> 46:51.517
"TRAPPED IN WRONG ANSWERS" AFTER-PARTY

46:52.684 --> 46:53.894
-Hello.
-Hello.

46:53.977 --> 46:56.980
-Why didn't Director Park Gyeong-se come?
-He was up all night, so he's sleeping.

46:57.064 --> 46:59.107
That's a shame. I had a lot to ask him.

47:00.609 --> 47:01.443
Okay, then.

47:04.780 --> 47:07.658
Does your company produce
period pieces as well?

47:07.741 --> 47:08.867
Wait.

47:14.081 --> 47:15.082
Director Park!

47:15.582 --> 47:16.625
Why are you so late?

47:16.708 --> 47:18.710
I was tired so I almost didn't make it.

47:18.794 --> 47:19.711
Oh, really?

47:20.337 --> 47:21.421
Have you eaten?

47:22.714 --> 47:24.049
Please excuse me for a second.

47:28.178 --> 47:30.013
-Feels like quite the party.
-Please dig in.

47:30.973 --> 47:31.932
Oh, hello.

47:32.933 --> 47:35.102
It's very interesting, huh?

47:35.185 --> 47:36.395
Isn't it weird, though?

47:36.478 --> 47:37.938
But I think it'll do well.

47:38.021 --> 47:39.356
Are you sure about that?

47:52.119 --> 47:54.204
Oh, it's Ms. Ko.

47:55.247 --> 47:56.331
Ms. Ko!

48:11.638 --> 48:12.598
When did you get here?

48:16.393 --> 48:17.519
Who are you, sir?

48:18.103 --> 48:19.938
Come on. Are you drunk?

48:20.522 --> 48:21.481
Do you know me?

48:23.734 --> 48:25.235
I don't think we've met before.

48:26.862 --> 48:29.281
What are you doing?
What's with the acting?

48:29.364 --> 48:32.784
Excuse me, but I don't know who you are.

48:33.410 --> 48:36.163
I believe you've got the wrong person.
Can you please leave?

48:38.332 --> 48:40.375
Director Park,
I thought you couldn't come.

48:43.003 --> 48:45.464
Episodes three and four are amazing!

48:46.089 --> 48:47.633
They're more fun than the first two.

48:47.716 --> 48:49.176
That's good to hear.

48:49.259 --> 48:51.595
Everyone in the company is raving about
how National Stress Management Department

48:51.678 --> 48:54.097
has been confirmed
as a long-running series.

48:55.390 --> 48:57.976
You have to sign
a three-season deal with us, okay?

48:58.060 --> 48:59.936
Goodness, three seasons? Come on.

49:00.896 --> 49:02.481
-Just think about it.
-I will.

49:06.693 --> 49:07.736
Excuse me.

49:08.320 --> 49:10.656
Are you Director Park Gyeong-se who wrote
National Stress Management Department?

49:12.574 --> 49:14.660
So you're the one who wrote that.

49:14.743 --> 49:17.954
I'm so sorry for not recognizing you.

49:18.038 --> 49:19.956
Why are you acting like this?

49:21.500 --> 49:23.502
I really enjoyed reading it.

49:24.086 --> 49:25.754
I've read all of your work,

49:27.172 --> 49:30.467
but I think this is your best yet.

49:31.426 --> 49:32.344
I'm sure it'll do well.

49:40.310 --> 49:41.978
Your writing

49:42.062 --> 49:43.480
was full of excitement.

49:44.147 --> 49:45.107
So full of energy!

49:51.947 --> 49:53.532
You must be in love.

50:05.377 --> 50:07.254
Your writing was full of excitement.

50:10.924 --> 50:14.261
For creators,
people are their greatest asset.

50:15.429 --> 50:19.391
Like slash-and-burn farmers
who burn their land to cultivate again,

50:20.100 --> 50:21.977
creators can completely fall for someone

50:23.145 --> 50:24.438
and soak up their words,

50:25.147 --> 50:26.398
their energy,

50:26.481 --> 50:30.485
and everything about them
to get back on their feet.

50:31.653 --> 50:32.988
That's why I think

50:33.572 --> 50:37.701
creators should be allowed to fall in love
a hundred, a thousand times.

50:42.622 --> 50:43.707
I'll support you.

50:44.708 --> 50:47.377
Keep writing with that same excitement
to the very end.

50:48.044 --> 50:48.879
Good luck.

50:56.803 --> 50:57.679
Honey.

51:00.265 --> 51:01.224
Hye-jin.

51:02.434 --> 51:03.810
Damn it.

51:04.936 --> 51:05.812
Ko Hye-jin.

51:14.488 --> 51:15.989
They say the most pitiful person…

51:18.158 --> 51:19.451
is the wife of a director.

51:21.578 --> 51:22.662
But I'm also…

51:24.623 --> 51:26.333
the CEO of a production company.

51:32.297 --> 51:33.590
So be excited.

51:35.634 --> 51:38.053
Keep being excited.

51:40.305 --> 51:41.598
Just write well.

51:43.141 --> 51:45.227
I don't care if you fall into hell

51:46.895 --> 51:48.480
or into a honeypot.

51:52.317 --> 51:54.611
As long as you come back
with some writing,

51:54.694 --> 51:57.906
I'll drag you into hell or shove you
straight into that damn honeypot myself!

52:03.787 --> 52:06.289
So just keep being excited.

52:14.589 --> 52:16.091
Fine, I got excited!

52:17.300 --> 52:20.262
I met a woman who looked at me
the way Ko Hye-jin used to,

52:20.345 --> 52:21.805
so I got excited!

52:28.353 --> 52:30.689
You don't even dote on me anymore!

52:31.439 --> 52:32.941
So how do you expect me to write?

52:55.922 --> 52:57.507
I didn't know what to do,

52:58.383 --> 53:00.010
so I got hammered and went to sleep.

53:01.928 --> 53:02.971
When I got up,

53:03.847 --> 53:05.098
it was dark outside.

53:07.350 --> 53:08.894
Depression presses down on me

53:10.437 --> 53:11.438
like a heavy iron weight.

53:21.740 --> 53:24.993
Who the hell are you
to object to casting Oh Jeong-hui?

53:25.744 --> 53:28.079
You even went behind my back
and told Mr. Choi that you're Yeong-sil.

53:29.372 --> 53:31.166
I'm scrapping this. I won't do it.

53:31.249 --> 53:32.792
I won't!

53:32.876 --> 53:35.003
Speak slowly. I'll hear you out.

53:35.503 --> 53:37.047
The more you run your mouth,

53:38.256 --> 53:39.424
the better it is for me

53:40.383 --> 53:41.468
since I'm recording this.

53:44.387 --> 53:45.889
Overconfident bastard.

53:47.140 --> 53:49.476
You're working on a project
worth hundreds of billions of won

53:49.559 --> 53:51.728
with a bunch of A-list actors,

53:51.811 --> 53:54.105
and you make a call like this
without thinking?

53:55.106 --> 53:57.317
Your voice needs to be
kept on record forever,

53:58.443 --> 54:00.028
so the world never forgets

54:01.571 --> 54:02.739
what kind of person you are.

54:03.239 --> 54:04.407
Someone like you

54:05.241 --> 54:06.785
never should've been born.

54:26.763 --> 54:27.931
Don't come.

54:29.182 --> 54:31.935
The food here is fine. Just get some rest.

54:33.269 --> 54:34.312
I'll go tomorrow.

54:35.355 --> 54:36.189
Lie down.

54:37.065 --> 54:38.233
Go on, lie down.

54:39.859 --> 54:41.069
Watch some TV.

54:41.945 --> 54:42.821
Okay?

55:11.975 --> 55:13.268
I have to give it to you.

55:13.351 --> 55:15.770
You've got a knack for picking up
whatever I throw away.

55:15.854 --> 55:19.024
You picked up Noh Kang-sik, the grant,

55:19.107 --> 55:20.442
and Byeon Eun-a.

55:21.067 --> 55:23.695
Shouldn't you be thanking me
at this point?

55:27.157 --> 55:29.617
You think you sound cool
saying you threw them away?

55:30.493 --> 55:31.911
Just be honest.

55:33.830 --> 55:34.873
You were afraid,

55:35.540 --> 55:36.499
so you deliberately

55:37.125 --> 55:38.293
let go of them.

55:39.669 --> 55:41.463
She shone so brightly,

55:42.213 --> 55:44.007
and you got so scared

55:45.383 --> 55:46.384
that you deliberately

55:47.052 --> 55:49.137
let go of Byeon Eun-a.

55:51.181 --> 55:52.182
Who got scared?

55:55.060 --> 55:56.144
Who shines?

55:58.271 --> 55:59.439
Who?

55:59.939 --> 56:02.817
-Tell me.
-I'm freaking scared too.

56:04.694 --> 56:05.987
But I endure it.

56:06.071 --> 56:08.031
Even if I go blind

56:08.114 --> 56:09.908
from her shiny brightness,

56:10.533 --> 56:12.410
I'm going to keep both eyes open
and endure it.

56:12.994 --> 56:15.997
That's the respect you owe someone
who believes in you, you jackass.

56:16.081 --> 56:17.832
No matter how scared you were,

56:18.541 --> 56:21.711
you shouldn't have turned so evil
when you ran away from her first!

56:21.795 --> 56:23.004
Goddamn it!

56:25.632 --> 56:27.801
Freaking loser. Who do you think you are?

57:05.505 --> 57:07.757
To hell with my movie.

57:08.341 --> 57:10.802
If I don't take you on today,
I'm a freaking moron.

57:42.041 --> 57:43.877
I'll kill you!

57:53.845 --> 57:54.846
Damn it.

57:57.599 --> 57:59.726
You think Byeon Eun-a is someone
you can just throw away?

58:00.435 --> 58:03.521
You can't throw away an ideal
sent by the gods!

58:03.605 --> 58:04.731
You can't!

58:16.075 --> 58:17.785
Just say, "Byeon Eun-a did it!"

58:17.869 --> 58:19.579
"Byeon Eun-a did it!"

58:19.662 --> 58:22.499
Cover the whole world with Byeon Eun-a!

58:22.582 --> 58:25.043
That's the only way
you can escape the hell you're in!

58:39.432 --> 58:40.767
I did it!

58:43.895 --> 58:45.188
I did it!

58:45.271 --> 58:47.315
I'm the one who did it!

58:58.743 --> 58:59.702
By the way,

59:00.703 --> 59:02.247
I'm really sorry to say this,

59:03.581 --> 59:05.792
but why does your identity
as Oh Jeong-hui's hidden daughter,

59:06.668 --> 59:09.254
something you find so painful,

59:10.588 --> 59:13.383
feel and look so shiny and bright to me?

59:19.556 --> 59:22.517
I'm just an ordinary person
who can never catch up to you.

59:24.811 --> 59:25.812
Ms. Byeon Eun-a.

59:26.771 --> 59:27.689
It seems

59:28.523 --> 59:30.900
you're determined to rise to the heavens.

59:45.623 --> 59:46.583
God.

59:53.548 --> 59:54.966
Please dote on me.

01:01:25.973 --> 01:01:30.061
CLOSED UNTIL THE END OF DECEMBER

01:01:56.754 --> 01:01:57.588
What happened?

01:01:58.965 --> 01:02:00.174
I was duped.

01:02:03.594 --> 01:02:04.512
This leather…

01:02:08.599 --> 01:02:10.935
was made in 1998.

01:02:14.939 --> 01:02:16.232
The story

01:02:16.816 --> 01:02:18.651
about it being worn
by a Russian soldier in World War II…

01:02:20.403 --> 01:02:21.571
was a lie.

01:02:22.029 --> 01:02:22.864
A lie.

01:02:28.745 --> 01:02:33.207
I thought about the Russian soldier
who was shot and killed

01:02:33.291 --> 01:02:35.501
and spent my days living
with a tragic sense of purpose.

01:02:38.045 --> 01:02:40.298
But I got duped by a handsome guy
at a flea market.

01:02:43.593 --> 01:02:45.887
It turns out, even handsome guys lie.

01:02:51.809 --> 01:02:52.643
But you know what?

01:02:54.520 --> 01:02:55.438
For some reason…

01:02:57.106 --> 01:02:58.483
I feel relieved.

01:03:01.152 --> 01:03:03.613
I think my life will be
one big comedy to the end,

01:03:04.405 --> 01:03:05.364
so I feel relieved.

01:03:10.495 --> 01:03:12.330
The protagonist in Joker

01:03:12.413 --> 01:03:14.540
thought his life was a tragedy,

01:03:14.624 --> 01:03:17.210
but when he found it was a comedy,
he went off the rails.

01:03:17.293 --> 01:03:18.169
However…

01:03:20.296 --> 01:03:21.255
I like

01:03:21.881 --> 01:03:22.715
that it's a comedy.

01:03:27.678 --> 01:03:29.514
Life should be a comedy.

01:03:31.307 --> 01:03:34.560
Would you mind
if I did a classic comedy bit?

01:03:41.734 --> 01:03:42.985
Guess where my tooth is?

01:03:46.781 --> 01:03:48.074
It only feels right to do this

01:03:48.741 --> 01:03:50.284
since I've lost my tooth.

01:04:18.312 --> 01:04:20.106
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

01:04:38.249 --> 01:04:40.626
Just so you know,
it's not just women at Eun-a's house.

01:04:41.210 --> 01:04:43.754
If you mess with Eun-a,
you'll be in real trouble.

01:04:43.838 --> 01:04:44.922
Let's just stop, Dong-man.

01:04:45.006 --> 01:04:47.383
I was just saying it for fun.

01:04:47.466 --> 01:04:49.093
Let's end this. Damn it.

01:04:49.176 --> 01:04:51.679
You can probably do it
without the emotion watch now.

01:04:51.762 --> 01:04:52.763
You should give it a try.

01:04:52.847 --> 01:04:55.141
Practice accurately identifying emotions.

01:04:55.224 --> 01:04:56.309
Why isn't Writer Park here?

01:04:56.893 --> 01:04:59.145
Just ignore me and keep writing
with that same excitement.

01:05:00.980 --> 01:05:03.190
I'm Director Hwang Dong-man.

01:05:03.858 --> 01:05:05.985
Dong-man has gone quiet.

01:05:06.068 --> 01:05:07.320
I think he's having a mental breakdown.

01:05:08.154 --> 01:05:09.739
Start filming already, you bastard!

01:05:09.822 --> 01:05:10.865
Start filming!

01:05:15.828 --> 01:05:20.833
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
